     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "Socrates’s main theories put moral considerations above all others. Additionally, his main philosophy revolved around the idea of self-knowledge and the pursuit of truth and virtue. His famous saying was “know thyself,” which emphasizes the importance of looking inside and understanding one’s own beliefs, values, and limitations. When you understand those, you can live a good and virtuous life."
